# This repo is checked out with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. That is harmless for source files but fatal for the baseline, which
# tests/check_baseline.py compares as an exact string: a CRLF-translated file can
# never match rich's LF output, and the gate would fail forever with an
# invisible cause.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion for the file, in both directions.
tests/baseline/dashboard.txt -text

# The baseline also carries SIGNIFICANT TRAILING WHITESPACE (rich centres table
# titles by padding them). Editors set to strip trailing whitespace on save, or
# a pre-commit hook that does, will silently rewrite it and break the gate.
# Nothing in git can prevent that -- it is an editor setting -- so it is called
# out in tests/baseline/README.md too. If the gate starts failing on lines that
# look identical, diff the trailing spaces first.

# Keep normal sources LF in the repo, however they sit in the working tree.
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
